{
  "contract": [
    "1. One logical provider set: exactly one set of quota provider ids; each surface list is a view of it, stated in this manifest (id, display name, per-surface presence).",
    "2. Landed only when landed everywhere: a new provider lands web fetcher + registration, VS Code fetcher + dispatch + configured entry, UI catalog + type, and the docs row in the same change; a surface that legitimately cannot serve a provider records a named exception with a reason in this manifest \u2014 never a silent absence.",
    "3. Aliases are not providers: a credential alias (openai for codex) is recorded as an alias and appears in no surface provider list.",
    "4. Configured and fetch select through one function: per provider per backend, exactly one credential-selection function serves both the configured predicate and the fetch path.",
    "5. No distinct id for a duplicate fetcher: a behaviour-identical fetcher id is folded into its provider (alias / folded instance) or registered with the distinct data it adds stated."
  ],
  "design": "https://github.com/developing-today-forks/openchamber/issues/1808",
  "issue": "https://github.com/developing-today-forks/openchamber/issues/1809",
  "surfaces": [
    "web",
    "vscode_dispatch",
    "vscode_configured",
    "ui_catalog",
    "ui_union",
    "docs"
  ],
